1578 ( [LINK: (MDLXXVIII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_numerals] ) was a  [LINK: (common year starting on Wednesday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Wednesday]  in the  [LINK: (Julian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_calendar] .


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (January 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_13]  – The  [LINK: (Siege of Gvozdansko) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Gvozdansko]  ends in the  [LINK: (Kingdom of Croatia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Croatia_(Habsburg)]  as Ottoman Empire troops led by  [LINK: (Ferhad Pasha Sokolović) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferhad_Pasha_Sokolovi%C4%87]  capture the fortress at  [LINK: (Gvozdansko) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gvozdansko] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (January 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31]  –  [LINK: (Battle of Gembloux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Gembloux_(1578)] : Spanish forces under  [LINK: (Don John of Austria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Austria]  and  [LINK: (Alexander Farnese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Farnese,_Duke_of_Parma]  defeat the Dutch; Farnese begins to recover control of the French-speaking  [LINK: (Southern Netherlands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Netherlands] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-2]

[LINK: (February 6) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_6]  –  [LINK: (Pope Gregory XIII) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Gregory_XIII]  issues the papal bull Illius fulti praesidio and creates the  [LINK: (Diocese of Manila) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Catholic_Archdiocese_of_Manila] , the first Roman Catholic diocese in the Philippines, with  [LINK: (Domingo de Salazar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domingo_de_Salazar]  as the first Bishop of Manila. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-3]  The diocese will be raised to the status of archdiocese on August 14, 1595.

[LINK: (February 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_8]  – The city council of Amsterdam in the Netherlands ratifies a treaty placing the city under the authority of  [LINK: (Willem, Prince of Orange) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_the_Silent] , and joining the  [LINK: (States of Holland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/States_of_Holland_and_West_Friesland] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (February 12) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_12]  –  [LINK: (Mohammad Khodabanda) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammad_Khodabanda] , older brother of the late  [LINK: (Shah Ismail II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismail_II] , begins his reign as the new  [LINK: (Shah) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_monarchs_of_Persia]  of  [LINK: (Persia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safavid_dynasty]  (now Iran) after entering the Persian capital at  [LINK: (Qazvin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qazvin] , after removing his sister  [LINK: (Pari Khan Khanum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pari_Khan_Khanum] , who had exercised regal authority after Ismail's death. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-5]  His first act as ruler is to have Pari Khan Khanum strangled to death.

[LINK: (February 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_13]  – Two days after the Battle of Gembloux, Spanish troops capture the city of  [LINK: (Leuven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leuven] , forcing Willem, Prince of Orange, to flee  [LINK: (Brussels) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brussels]  and relocate to  [LINK: (Antwerp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antwerp] .Geoffrey Parker, The Dutch Revolt (Cornell University Press, 1977) p.186

[LINK: (March 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_11]  –  [LINK: (Nicolò da Ponte) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicol%C3%B2_da_Ponte]  is elected as the new  [LINK: (Doge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doge_of_Venice]  of the Republic of Venice after 44 ballots, following the March 3 death of  [LINK: (Sebastiano Venier) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastiano_Venier] . [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (March 20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_20] 
 [LINK: (James Douglas, 4th Earl of Morton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Douglas,_4th_Earl_of_Morton] , the last of the regents for King James VI of Scotland, resigns after having served as regent since November 24, 1572.
The Belgian city of  [LINK: (Bruges) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruges] , controlled by Spain, falls to Dutch rebels. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-7]

[LINK: (James Douglas, 4th Earl of Morton) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Douglas,_4th_Earl_of_Morton] , the last of the regents for King James VI of Scotland, resigns after having served as regent since November 24, 1572.

The Belgian city of  [LINK: (Bruges) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruges] , controlled by Spain, falls to Dutch rebels. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-7]

[LINK: (April 23) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_23]  – (17th day of 3rd month, Tensho 6) The  [LINK: (Siege of Otate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Otate]  begins in Japan after the death of  [LINK: (Uesugi Kenshin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uesugi_Kenshin] , the warlord of the  [LINK: (Echigo Province) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echigo_Province] .

[LINK: (April 27) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_27]  – The  [LINK: (Duel of the Mignons) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_of_the_Mignons]  claims the lives of two favorites of  [LINK: (Henry III of France) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_III_of_France] , and two favourites of  [LINK: (Henry I, Duke of Guise) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I,_Duke_of_Guise] . [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (May 26) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May_26]  – The  [LINK: (Alteratie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alteratie]  takes place in  [LINK: (Amsterdam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amsterdam] , expelling the 24 Catholic members of the 40-man city government, and forming a new council is formed with 30 Calvinist Protestants and 10 Catholics.

[LINK: (May 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May_31]  –  [LINK: (Martin Frobisher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Frobisher]  sails from  [LINK: (Harwich) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harwich]  in England with 15 ships to North America, where he will arrive at  [LINK: (Frobisher Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frobisher_Bay]  in July on his third expedition.

[LINK: (June 11) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_11]  –  [LINK: (Humphrey Gilbert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humphrey_Gilbert]  is granted  [LINK: (letters patent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Letters_patent]  from the English crown to establish a colony in  [LINK: (North America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_America] . [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (June 20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_20]  – The Frobisher expedition reaches  [LINK: (Greenland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland] .

[LINK: (June 30) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_30]  – After having come into conflict on May 17 with his fellow officer,  [LINK: (Thomas Doughty) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Doughty_(explorer)] , during their circumnavigation of the world,  [LINK: (Francis Drake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Drake]  puts Doughty on trial while the flagship Pelican is docked at what is now Argentina. A jury of sailors convicts Doughty of treason and attempted mutiny. Doughty is beheaded on July 2. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-10]

[LINK: (July 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_2]  – The Frobisher expedition reaches Canada and enters what is now  [LINK: (Frobisher Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frobisher_Bay] . One of the ships, the Dennis, is wrecked on an iceberg.

[LINK: (July 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_31] 
At the  [LINK: (Battle of Rijmenam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Rijmenam_(1578)] , fought near  [LINK: (Antwerp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antwerp]  in what is now  [LINK: (Belgium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgium] , a combined Dutch and English force under the command of the Count of Boussu and England's John Norreys defeats Spanish troops commanded by  [LINK: (Don Juan de Austria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Austria] .
According to some accounts, Englishman  [LINK: (Martin Frobisher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Frobisher]  holds the first  [LINK: (Thanksgiving) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thanksgiving]  celebration by Europeans in Canada, on  [LINK: (Newfoundland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfoundland_(island)] , after he and his fleet encounter two ships that they feared had been lost. However, the celebration involves no feast and is limited to a sermon by the expedition's minister and Frobisher's men giving praise. [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-11]  [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-12]

At the  [LINK: (Battle of Rijmenam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Rijmenam_(1578)] , fought near  [LINK: (Antwerp) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antwerp]  in what is now  [LINK: (Belgium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgium] , a combined Dutch and English force under the command of the Count of Boussu and England's John Norreys defeats Spanish troops commanded by  [LINK: (Don Juan de Austria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Austria] .

According to some accounts, Englishman  [LINK: (Martin Frobisher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Frobisher]  holds the first  [LINK: (Thanksgiving) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thanksgiving]  celebration by Europeans in Canada, on  [LINK: (Newfoundland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newfoundland_(island)] , after he and his fleet encounter two ships that they feared had been lost. However, the celebration involves no feast and is limited to a sermon by the expedition's minister and Frobisher's men giving praise. [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-11]  [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-12]

[LINK: (August 4) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_4]  – King  [LINK: (Sebastian of Portugal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_of_Portugal]  is killed in the  [LINK: (Battle of Alcácer Quibir) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Alc%C3%A1cer_Quibir]  in North Africa while fighting the  [LINK: (Saadi Sultanate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saadi_Sultanate] . Sebastian's elderly uncle,  [LINK: (Cardinal Henry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry,_King_of_Portugal] , is named as the heir to the throne, initiating a succession crisis in Portugal.

[LINK: (August 20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_20] – [LINK: (September 6) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_6]  – After renaming this flagship, Pelican to the Golden Hind,  [LINK: (Francis Drake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Drake]  and his fleet begin their passage through the  [LINK: (Strait of Magellan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Magellan] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-GoldenHind-13]

[LINK: (August 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_31]  – The Forbisher expedition departs North America for its journey back to England.

[LINK: (September 6) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_6]  – After 16 days travel, the fleet of Francis Drake completes its traverse of the  [LINK: (Strait of Magellan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Magellan]  between the tip of South America and  [LINK: (Tierra del Fuego) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tierra_del_Fuego] . Upon entering the  [LINK: (Pacific Ocean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Ocean] , the fleet encounters violent storms. The supply ship Marigold, with over 100 men under the command of John Thomas, is lost with all hands off of  [LINK: (Cape Horn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Horn] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-GoldenHind-13]  The rest of the fleet continues its  [LINK: (voyage around the world) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Drake%27s_circumnavigation] .

[LINK: (October 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_1]  –  [LINK: (Alessandro Farnese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Farnese,_Duke_of_Parma]  succeeds his uncle,  [LINK: (Don John) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Austria] , as  [LINK: (Governor of the Spanish Netherlands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_the_Spanish_Netherlands] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-BrulezKoch2012-14]

[LINK: (October 21) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_21]  –  [LINK: (Battle of Wenden) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battles_of_Wenden_(1577%E2%80%9378)] : The Russians are defeated by the  [LINK: (Swedes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweden] , who proceed to take  [LINK: (Polotsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polotsk] .

[LINK: (November 19) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November_19]  –  [LINK: (Humphrey Gilbert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humphrey_Gilbert]  and  [LINK: (Walter Ralegh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Ralegh]  set out from  [LINK: (Plymouth) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plymouth]  in England, leading an expedition to establish a colony in North America. They will be forced to turn back six months later. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-CBH-15]

[LINK: (December 9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/December_9]  – After more than five years of combat in southern France, the Protestant Huguenot citadel of  [LINK: (Ménerbes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A9nerbes]  negotiates a surrender to its French Catholic attackers. [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-16]

[LINK: (Battle of the Spoiling Dyke) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Spoiling_Dyke]  at  [LINK: (Trumpan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpan]  on the Scottish  [LINK: (Isle of Skye) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isle_of_Skye] : the  [LINK: (Clan MacLeod) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_MacLeod]  are victorious over the  [LINK: (MacDonalds of Uist) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Donald]  in a feud. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1578#cite_note-17]

The  [LINK: (Ottoman Empire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman_Empire]  conquers  [LINK: (Abkhazia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abkhazia] .

[LINK: (Sarsa Dengel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarsa_Dengel] ,  [LINK: (Emperor of Ethiopia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_of_Ethiopia] , defeats and kills  [LINK: (Bahr negus Yeshaq) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahr_negus_Yeshaq]  along with his Ottoman allies, finally ending his rebellion.

Sonam Gyrso receives from Prince Atlan Khan the title of Talaï, and becomes the third  [LINK: (Dalai Lama) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalai_Lama]  of  [LINK: (Tibet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibet] .

The last outbreak of  [LINK: (sweating sickness) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweating_sickness]  occurs in England.

The  [LINK: (Portuguese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_Empire]  assist Lord  [LINK: (Ōmura Sumitada) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%8Cmura_Sumitada] , the first Christian Japanese daimyo, in repulsing an assault on  [LINK: (Nagasaki) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagasaki]  by the  [LINK: (Ryūzōji clan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ry%C5%ABz%C5%8Dji_clan] .

[LINK: (Fur trade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_American_fur_trade]  begins in Newfoundland in North America.


